      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Palmer Park, named for U.S. Senator Palmer, sits between Longfellow and Edison Avenues, a green heart of the neighborhood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.detroithistorical.org/learn/online-research/encyclopedia-of-detroit/boston-edison-historic-district",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Joseph’s Episcopal Church on Woodward Avenue showcases Gothic architecture and has long served as a cultural anchor for Boston–Edison.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://bostonedisondetroitneighborhood.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Historic Boston–Edison Association, founded in 1921, is the city’s oldest continuous neighborhood association.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
